# Rust
/target
/_site/
# Cargo.lock IS committed: rush is a binary/application workspace, so the lock
# must be checked in for reproducible builds. allocative 0.3.6 breaks
# starlark_map 0.12.0 (RawTable: Allocative unsatisfied) — a fresh clone with
# no lock floats to the broken combo and fails to compile. Pinning here keeps
# `git clone && cargo build` working and lets main build TensorFlow.
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build outputs
/output/
/bazel-*
/rush-out/
/rush-bin

# Logs (general exclusion)
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.orig
*.rej
.ai-traces/

# Build artifacts
compile_commands.json
.build-state.json

# Cache directories
.cache/
.rush-cache/
external/

# Test artifacts
examples/tensorflow_scale_test/bzl_segments/
